From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Set client opacity from swapchain alpha mode.

The Vulkan alpha callback introduced by Erhan Bilgili already records whether
the swapchain uses alpha, but the client wl_surface itself keeps an empty
opaque region. The flag only affects the parent carrier and stacking policy.

Make the client's opaque-region optimization hint agree with the requested
swapchain alpha mode. The parent carrier is a separate surface and may need
to remain transparent for GDI content. An opaque region is not an instruction
to rewrite buffer alpha, and is not required for correct opaque-buffer
rendering by the compositor.

Apply the swapchain alpha mode to the client surface's opaque region, without
changing the parent carrier, stacking, or child-rendering policy. Use a
surface-local region covering every possible surface size, which Wayland
clips to the surface, so resizing and fractional scaling need no updates.
Clear the region again for alpha-enabled swapchains, including cached surface
reuse. Apply this even when has_alpha was already FALSE on a new surface.

Leave the state pending for the next WSI buffer commit. An extra commit here
could publish unrelated pending surface state during swapchain recreation.
This is driver-independent and does not force transparent swapchains opaque.

Follow-up testing in #786 confirmed these requests reach the Vulkan client
surface, but did not fix the reported HDR transparency. Marjinoz corrected
the original format diagnosis: the buffers were already XBGR16161616F
(XB4H), not ABGR16161616F (AB4H), including before this patch. Keep this as
explicit opacity metadata, not as a confirmed fix for #786 or an NVIDIA
buffer-format workaround.

Reported-by: Marjinoz (https://github.com/Marjinoz)
Link: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/786
Link: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/786#issuecomment-5752918615
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -5319,8 +5319,26 @@ void wayland_client_surface_set_alpha(struct client_surface *client, BOOL alpha)
 {
     struct wayland_client_surface *surface = impl_from_client_surface(client);
+    struct wl_region *region = NULL;
+
     surface->has_alpha = alpha;
+
+    if (!alpha)
+    {
+        if (!(region = wl_compositor_create_region(process_wayland.wl_compositor)))
+        {
+            ERR("Failed to create client opaque region\n");
+            return;
+        }
+        /* Surface-local regions are clipped by the compositor. Cover future
+         * resizes as well, independently of buffer scale and viewport size. */
+        wl_region_add(region, 0, 0, INT32_MAX, INT32_MAX);
+    }
+
+    /* Let the next WSI buffer commit apply the pending opacity state. */
+    wl_surface_set_opaque_region(surface->wl_surface, region);
+    if (region) wl_region_destroy(region);
 }
 
 /**********************************************************************
  *          wayland_surface_ensure_contents
  *
